Roland, this is Ardsley's written direction on SR-014, confirmed by our exe=
cutive committee on May 16. A signed copy on Ardsley letterhead is attached=
.<br />
<br />
Ardsley Financial Group directs VAA to delete Section 09 05 61 in its entir=
ety from the 632588 contract documents, across floors 12 through 19, and to=
 issue the corresponding ASI so that Thackston Bell can proceed. We accept =
the credit of $347,900 and the 18 day schedule recovery.<br />
<br />
Ardsley acknowledges that this is an owner-directed deletion made over VAA'=
s written recommendation of April 6, 2011, that VAA advised against it on t=
he basis of the in-situ relative humidity testing, and that Ardsley relied =
on the independent assessment prepared by Prewitt Building Science in reach=
ing this decision. Ardsley accepts responsibility for the consequences of t=
he deletion, including any future flooring performance issues arising from =
slab moisture, and will not look to VAA on account of this direction.<br />
<br />
I appreciate that you put your position in writing rather than letting this=
 happen in a meeting. For the record, I think you may well be right. The co=
mmittee decided the schedule anyway.
